WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.835
-Our first guest is a four-time

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:06.272
Emmy-nominated actress for her
work on "Game of Thrones."

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.373
She's also --
-Whoo!

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:09.676
-Yeah! Oww!
She's also co-written

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:13.112
this new comic book called
"M.O.M. Mother of Madness."

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:17.250
The first issue came out today.
Here is Emilia Clarke!

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.785
Hey! Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:19.819
That's what I'm talking about!

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.122
Hey, bud!
-Hi!

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:25.358
-Emilia, it is so great
to see you.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.226
I can't wait to talk about this.

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:29.462
I know we discussed it
maybe last time you were, like,

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.131
you were working on
or had this idea.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.198
I know a lot of work
went into this.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.566
-Yes.
-Congratulations. It's out.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.802
Officially today.
-Thank you so much.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.070
-Yeah.
-It's the strangest thing.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.872
Thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.574
-You've done a lot of cool
things since you've been here,

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.010
by the way.
You went skydiving.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.444
-Yes.
-Which, uh...

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:47.947
Here's a photo of you
mid air skydiving.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.984
Now -- Now what would
make you want to do this?

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.752
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.987
You still look good
even skydiving.

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:56.355
Yeah, but I mean --
-You're lying.

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.658
-No, I'm not.
How did --

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.827
What made you want to do this?

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.629
-Okay. So basically,
this was for my birthday.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:06.031
And I thought, "Okay.
I'm turning 34,"

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:08.601
which at that point,
now it's not scary,

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.269
but at the time, it was --

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:12.972
I couldn't even fathom the idea
that I would turn 34.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.408
So, I thought I would do
something that was 10 times

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:18.177
scarier than turning 34, which
was jumping out of a plane.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:21.080
-How was the person
strapped to you?

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.582
-Yeah.
-What's that all about?

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.950
And do you get
to interview them?

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.985
Do you know them before
they're strapped to you?

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.954
Do they talk to you?
-No.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.355
-You don't know them?
-No.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.757
-Okay.
So did you get, like, a --

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.091
Did you get a good pairing?

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.626
Did you get a wacky guy
or something?

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.661
I don't want a guy going like,
"3, 2..." and then

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:37.196
pulls the rip cord,
and you go...

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.299
You know, or does the thing like
"On the count of five.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.000
5, 4..."
and then pulls the thing.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.502
And you go --
That's not funny to me.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.637
I don't know.
How was he?

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.873
-So, my mom and my brother
were the only people

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:50.009
who came with me.
And my mom is not 34.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:53.480
And so I -- they get paired off
with their people.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.948
And my mom gets, like,
Chipper Mick,

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:59.752
kind of Scouts guy who, like,
is, you know, all over it.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.120
He's like the team leader.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.222
-My brother gets, like,
cool, serious guy,

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:04.523
who's taking it
really seriously.

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:07.627
-That's what I want.
-And I just get this guy

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.662
who's like "All right, luv,
let's go for it."

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.764
-Yeah, that's the crazy guy!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.365
That's who I would get.
-The crazy guy!

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.001
-The crazy guy who's like,
"Let's do it!

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.335
Oops!
I'm not strapped to you,

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:17.770
and I forgot the parachute,
dude!"

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.471
You know --
-That.

00:02:19.471 --> 00:02:20.873
-You got that guy.
-Exactly.

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:23.375
-You landed, and you were so
happy or mad or something.

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:25.178
You just
couldn't stop screaming.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.178
Look at you.
Just --

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:27.880
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.616
It was the biggest adrenaline
rush of my entire life.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.852
Also, just for future reference,
if you're gonna jump

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.821
out of a plane, don't take
the two most important people

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.323
in the world to you, because
when you're sitting there,

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.359
my mom, first of all,
turns around to me

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:42.128
as the door opens
and just goes, "Yeah!"

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.230
[ Laughter ]
I love my mom.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.931
-"I love you, Mom."
That's awesome.

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:48.534
That's so rad.
See? You'll never forget that.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.970
I want to --
I want to talk about now also

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.906
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.
-Yes.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:56.542
-You're now joining
the Marvel Universe

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:59.946
with this new --
with this new miniseries.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.781
-Yes.
-What can we say?

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:03.916
Can we say the name of it or no?

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:05.317
-Well, okay.
So, yeah.

00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:09.722
I'm pretty sure we can say
it's called "Secret Invasion."

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.391
-Okay.
-But I'm already scared.

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:15.894
The first people I spoke to from
Marvel were their security team.

00:03:15.894 --> 00:03:18.798
And I am convinced
there is a man outside my house.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:21.267
There's been a car parked there
for a long time.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.335
And I swear to God,
he's undercover.

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:25.571
-Yeah, yeah.
But I think they're like,

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:27.440
"Well, you're also good
at keeping good secrets

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.542
for 'Game of Thrones,'
so, like, she's used to it."

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:32.111
-That's not -- that's what I
thought, but they schooled me.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:35.247
And so --
I don't know what to do.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:37.416
-All right, all right.
Well, congrats on that.

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:38.784
I want to talk about this
right here.

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:40.619
This is --
You co-wrote this.

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:44.089
A new comic book called
"M.O.M. Mother of Madness."

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:46.458
-Yes.
-How did it come about?

00:03:46.458 --> 00:03:49.128
-Okay.
So it was just a silly idea.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:52.531
It was a silly conversation
that happened in a car

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:54.200
on our way to a gig
with friends.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.968
And we were like,
"Yeah, wouldn't it be funny

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.538
if there was a superhero
who wasn't perfect

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.639
and who was just
a big mess like us?"

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:02.441
And I was like,
"That would be really funny."

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:05.444
And, like, was anxious.
That would be really funny.

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:09.748
And then I went home
and just wrote that.

00:04:09.748 --> 00:04:11.717
So I wrote like
50 pages of this,

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.552
and this kind of character
just came out of me.

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:16.155
And I did all the other
characters and just a lot of --

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.824
There was a lot of material
that was ready to come out.

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:22.261
And, uh --
And now it's here.

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:24.330
And it's real thing.
-I mean, it's great.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:28.467
Do -- Do you meet with artists?
And how does it work?

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.369
-Yes. Yeah, yeah.
So now I know that there's

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:32.404
a lot of people that are
involved in making a comic.

00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:34.741
There's like 11 people
that it takes to make a comic.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:37.076
And I teamed up with
this incredible writer

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:40.480
called Marguerite Bennett,
who was my guru and my guide

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.882
'cause I didn't know the first
thing about making a comic.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.516
And so I wrote all the stuff,

00:04:44.516 --> 00:04:46.786
and then she turned it
into comic,

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.554
turned it into this thing.
-Yeah.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.790
Yeah, comic form.
-This beautiful thing.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.992
-It's gorgeous.
It's well-done.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.627
-Thank you. Thank you.
-It's fantastic.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:57.329
I mean, this is a big deal.
Do you think this could be

00:04:57.329 --> 00:05:00.566
turned into a movie
or a TV show?

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.235
-Well, okay. So here's the way
I feel about this.

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:05.938
It's not why I started.
It's not why I made a comic.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:11.410
I made a comic 'cause I'm crazy,
and so I did that.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.815
And if it's really crap
and no one wants it,

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.884
then it won't be a movie.
-No, that's not true, no.

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:20.886
Please, we all know that you --
-If it's good...

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:23.622
-We all know how sane you are.
I mean -- yeah.

00:05:23.622 --> 00:05:25.024
-There you go.
Yes.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.393
-I think this thing
is fantastic.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.228
You got to be really proud, bud.
Congratulations.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.663
This is awesome.
-Thank you.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:33.065
-Emilia Clarke.
"M.O.M. Mother of Madness"

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:35.068
is available now.
It is great.

